---
import ProjectLayout from '../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro';
---
<ProjectLayout title="Echo of Mobius" projectName="Echo of<br><br>Mobius" backHref="/selected-works-plain#project1">
    <ul slot="metadata">
        <li>Infinite Game with AI Characters</li>
        <li>Oct. 2024</li>
        <li style="color: #949494; margin-bottom: -1vw;">My Roles:</li>
        <li><dd> Team Lead / Game Design <br> Game Dev / AI & ML Dev </dd></li>
        <li style="color: #949494; margin-bottom: -1vw;">Project Type:</li>
        <li><dd> Startup </dd></li>
        <li style="color: #949494; margin-bottom: -1vw;">Core Tech Stacks:</li>
        <li><dd> Generative AI / Unity <br> Blender / Cloud Infra </dd></li>
    </ul>

    <div class="project">
        <img src="/assets/proj1.png" alt="Project 1">
        <h2>Nobody wants their AI companions stay in a chat box.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="project">
        <hr class="custom-line">
        <h3>Initiative</h3>
        <p>AI accompaniment is gradually becoming a part of more and more people's lives, and it has become a new content carrier. However, most AI companion apps on the market limit its potential to boring chat boxes.<br><br>As passionate gamers and early adopters of AI characters, my startup team launched this project to create an immersive game world where users can interact with AI characters in <b>more fun and engaging ways beyond chatting</b>. It features a <b>user-generated content ecosystem</b> that allows players to bring their imaginations to life while experiencing infinite content collectively created by the community.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="project">
        <h3>Research & Ideation</h3>
        <p>
            Our team started with a ton of market research. By "a ton," I mean we tried almost every AI chatbot app out there. We also spent hours daily in Reddit communities, joining discussions and interviewing users about why they quit or stayed hooked. Then, we explored role-playing games to find the best gameplay modes.</p>
        <img class="illustration" src="/assets/i1-1.png" style="margin-bottom: 6vh;"  alt="Ideation Images">
        <p>From our research, we found a significant overlap between AI chatbot users and RPG players. Both groups consist primarily of creative and imaginative young people and teenagers who are willing to treat virtual characters as real beings. Our surveys revealed <b>73%</b> of AI chatbot users seek deeper interactivity, while <b>68%</b> of RPG players expressed interest in AI-driven dynamic storytelling. It is clear that they expect the experience to become more immersive and interactive. Some AI chatbot users are beginning to lose interest due to <b>repetitive and simplistic</b> interactions. Based on these insights, we developed this simple user persona.</p>
        <img class="illustration" src="/assets/i1-2.png" alt="User Persona Images">
    </div>

    <div class="project">
        <h3>Prototyping</h3>
        <p>
            Building a full game is a huge effort, so we wanted to make sure we were on the right track first. Instead of diving straight in, we created a simple <b>Discord bot as our MVP</b>. With it, users could create and chat with characters, take them on text adventures, battle others (purely random winners), and watch them evolve. Our testers loved the community, and it grew quickly and organically.  Some played <b>4-5</b> hours a day for several days in a row, reaching level <b>400+</b>, which was way beyond our expectation. This small scale success validated the need for our project.
        </p>
        <img class="illustration" src="/assets/i1-3.png" alt="Discord Bot Images">
    </div>

    <div class="project">
        <h3>Product Development</h3>
        <p>
            With our MVP validating demand, we moved forward with building the game. From our market research, we identified <b>turn-based battles</b> and <b>CRPG text-pic adventures</b> as the best gameplay modes because of the broad audience and creative space, and are relatively simple to implement. We first developed a basic draft and recruited about 30 testers to help us refine visuals and balance gameplay mechanics.
            <br><br>
            On the technical side, the main challenge was integrating generative AI seamlessly into a production-level game. Our team of three 2D artists (including myself) created <b>130</b> virtual characters as a training dataset. We fine-tuned <b>SDXL</b> (later replaced with <b>Flux</b>) using LoRA techniques. To standardize the generated images, I developed a CV sequence algorithm that handled tasks like background removal, and adjustments to exposure, saturation, and size using techniques such as Gaussian blur or histogram equalization.
            <br><br>
            For character interactions, we used APIs from both OpenAI and Anthropic. GPT excelled at command interactions, while Claude generated more engaging narratives and dialogues. Each character was paired with a memory system designed by us to track player choices. For these memory systems, we employed <b>vector databases</b> to encode and retrieve past interactions, enabling characters to exhibit behavior influenced by historical player choices. To enhance immersion, we implemented <b>fixed-perspective 3D scenes</b> for the game's visuals.
        </p>
        <img class="illustration" src="/assets/i1-4.png" alt="Dev Log Images">
    </div>

    <div class="project">
        <h3>Growth & Operation</h3>
        <p>
            Our main growth strategy is collaborating with streamers. The game's creative freedom makes it easy for them to create engaging content, often leading to their <b>highest-ever CCV</b>. Many streamers promoted our game for free because of this. Additionally, the UGC ecosystem has driven organic growth, as players naturally share and expand the game themselves.
        </p>
        <img class="illustration" src="/assets/i1-5.png" alt="Streamer Images">
    </div>

    <div class="project">
        <h3>Outcome</h3>
        <p>
            • Launched in late October, now with <b>4,000+</b> users and <b>300+</b> paying players, still growing rapidly. It has established a sustainable business model with an impressive <b>90%</b> profit margin.<br><br>
            • Over <b>20,000</b> unique characters created, making it the game with the most playable characters worldwide.<br><br>
            • Achieved a second-week retention rate of <b>26%</b> and an average session time of <b>30+</b> minutes.<br><br>
            • Over <b>30</b> streamers featured the game, reaching <b>50k+</b> views across platforms.<br><br>
            • It has become the game with the <b>most playable characters</b> in the world, showcasing the transformative potential of generative AI technology in revolutionizing video games.
        </p>
    </div>
    <div class="project">
        <h3>Official Website: &ensp;<b><a href="https://www.echoofmobius.com" target="_blank" style="color: black;text-decoration: none;">www.echoofmobius.com</a></b></h3>
    </div>
    <div class="project">
        <h3>Gallery</h3>
        <div class="iframe-container">
            <iframe
            src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/izohRj-1sfM?si=lLVlqXmC7bcq8ca-"
            title="Echo of Mobius"
            frameborder="0"
            allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
            referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
            allowfullscreen>
            </iframe>
        </div>
        <img class="illustration" src="/assets/i1-6.png" alt="Gallary Images">
        <img class="illustration" src="/assets/i1-7.png" alt="Gallary Images">
        <img class="illustration" src="/assets/i1-8.png" alt="Gallary Images">
        <img class="illustration" src="/assets/i1-9.png" alt="Gallary Images">
    </div>
</ProjectLayout>
